Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes a structured error frame with the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Incremental Schema Mismatch Error",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["invalid_schema"]
    },
    "hint": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "checkpoint_cursor": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "resume_details": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "checkpoint_version": {
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "resume_token": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "resume_timestamp": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date-time"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed as a cyclic redundancy check (CRC) of the entire key-value pair represented by the resume token. The CRC algorithm used is the 32-bit CRC with a reflect-in-bit polynomial (CRC-32/IEEE). The CRC value is appended to the resume token as a base64-encoded string.
